WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.229 --> 00:00:03.710
When you're sculpting your terrain,

2
00:00:03.710 --> 00:00:06.830
the standard circle brush is very useful.

3
00:00:06.830 --> 00:00:08.689
However, there are gonna be instances

4
00:00:08.689 --> 00:00:10.910
where we would like to have more control

5
00:00:10.910 --> 00:00:13.230
over the brush that is used.

6
00:00:13.230 --> 00:00:15.070
And particular, what we would like to do

7
00:00:15.070 --> 00:00:17.570
in some instances is actually have a brush

8
00:00:17.570 --> 00:00:21.489
that resembles some type of landscape feature,

9
00:00:21.489 --> 00:00:24.910
some type of natural feature that we can then use

10
00:00:24.910 --> 00:00:27.629
to paint these features or apply these features

11
00:00:27.629 --> 00:00:29.309
to our landscape.

12
00:00:29.350 --> 00:00:34.189
And we can do this with our brush type being set to alpha

13
00:00:34.189 --> 00:00:38.909
and then setting our texture here to an alpha brush

14
00:00:38.909 --> 00:00:40.670
that we have imported.

15
00:00:40.670 --> 00:00:42.869
Now, before we go any further,

16
00:00:42.869 --> 00:00:46.009
let me show you what this actually can do.

17
00:00:46.009 --> 00:00:47.710
So if we come over here, look at this.

18
00:00:47.710 --> 00:00:49.509
This is alpha brushes in action.

19
00:00:49.509 --> 00:00:52.170
So here we have on the left-hand side,

20
00:00:52.170 --> 00:00:54.630
just that single alpha brush.

21
00:00:54.630 --> 00:00:58.469
And we've used that to create this one mountain here.

22
00:00:58.469 --> 00:01:02.820
And then if we use a combination of this brush

23
00:01:02.820 --> 00:01:04.920
in different areas and click at different strengths,

24
00:01:04.920 --> 00:01:06.540
we can actually get something like this

25
00:01:06.540 --> 00:01:09.859
that resembles a mountain range.

26
00:01:09.859 --> 00:01:12.420
So let's pop over to the editor and see how this works.

27
00:01:12.420 --> 00:01:14.219
So first, once I get inside the editor,

28
00:01:14.219 --> 00:01:16.579
I'm actually gonna come here, I'm gonna disable my fog

29
00:01:16.579 --> 00:01:18.180
so it makes things just a little bit easier

30
00:01:18.180 --> 00:01:19.540
for us to see.

31
00:01:19.540 --> 00:01:22.260
And then I'm gonna activate, well, before I do that,

32
00:01:22.260 --> 00:01:23.959
let's just hit control space really quick

33
00:01:23.959 --> 00:01:26.459
and make sure that we have this brushes folder

34
00:01:26.459 --> 00:01:29.400
and we have our impact craters and our mountain.

35
00:01:29.400 --> 00:01:33.840
We did import these at the beginning of our tutorial,

36
00:01:33.840 --> 00:01:35.340
but if you haven't, all you need to do

37
00:01:35.340 --> 00:01:38.480
is just simply grab these from the folder

38
00:01:38.480 --> 00:01:40.599
that accompanies this tutorial

39
00:01:40.599 --> 00:01:42.959
and then drag and drop these right

40
00:01:42.959 --> 00:01:45.040
into the content browser.

41
00:01:45.040 --> 00:01:47.000
You can put them inside of a folder called brushes

42
00:01:47.000 --> 00:01:47.819
or you could just leave them

43
00:01:47.819 --> 00:01:49.200
in the root of the content folder.

44
00:01:49.200 --> 00:01:50.920
That is entirely up to you.

45
00:01:50.920 --> 00:01:52.159
With those imported though,

46
00:01:52.159 --> 00:01:55.659
what I'm gonna do is come up now to my landscape

47
00:01:55.700 --> 00:01:56.780
and we're gonna come over here,

48
00:01:56.780 --> 00:01:58.299
make sure that sculpt is selected.

49
00:01:58.299 --> 00:01:59.780
And then in our brush type,

50
00:01:59.780 --> 00:02:03.280
we're gonna change this from our simple circular brush

51
00:02:03.280 --> 00:02:05.180
to our alpha brush.

52
00:02:05.180 --> 00:02:06.019
When we do that,

53
00:02:06.019 --> 00:02:07.980
we're gonna get a bunch of different brush settings.

54
00:02:07.980 --> 00:02:10.259
So really quickly, we have the texture,

55
00:02:10.259 --> 00:02:13.780
which is going to be the T mountain.

56
00:02:13.780 --> 00:02:14.659
So we're gonna use that

57
00:02:14.659 --> 00:02:16.759
and we're gonna use this selected asset

58
00:02:16.759 --> 00:02:18.139
from content browser.

59
00:02:18.139 --> 00:02:20.500
And then underneath this, we have a few other options.

60
00:02:20.500 --> 00:02:22.120
So we have our texture channel,

61
00:02:22.120 --> 00:02:24.900
which allows us to change the channel

62
00:02:24.900 --> 00:02:25.939
that is sampled from.

63
00:02:26.539 --> 00:02:29.460
So this means that we can actually store different masks

64
00:02:29.460 --> 00:02:32.699
or different textures inside of the R, G, B

65
00:02:32.699 --> 00:02:34.340
and alpha channels of a texture

66
00:02:34.340 --> 00:02:38.590
to give us more flexibility out of this one texture.

67
00:02:38.590 --> 00:02:40.969
For now though, we're just using the red channel

68
00:02:40.969 --> 00:02:43.110
because we only have one mask.

69
00:02:43.110 --> 00:02:44.629
We then have our brush size,

70
00:02:44.629 --> 00:02:46.530
which is gonna control the size of our brush

71
00:02:46.530 --> 00:02:48.330
that we edit the landscape with.

72
00:02:48.330 --> 00:02:49.909
And you can see it kind of right there.

73
00:02:49.909 --> 00:02:52.349
Then we have use clay brush and auto rotate

74
00:02:52.349 --> 00:02:53.949
as well as a texture rotation.

75
00:02:53.949 --> 00:02:55.069
Now for us, what we're gonna do

76
00:02:55.110 --> 00:02:57.189
is I'm actually gonna disable these two

77
00:02:57.189 --> 00:02:59.110
and I'm gonna take my brush here

78
00:02:59.110 --> 00:03:02.229
and just bring it all the way up to 81, 92.

79
00:03:02.229 --> 00:03:04.069
Now, if we were to go actually a little bit higher,

80
00:03:04.069 --> 00:03:04.909
check this out.

81
00:03:04.909 --> 00:03:06.189
If I multiply this by four,

82
00:03:06.189 --> 00:03:08.550
it's gonna give me a really massive brush,

83
00:03:08.550 --> 00:03:10.949
which I can't actually get by pulling that

84
00:03:10.949 --> 00:03:12.830
all the way to the right hand side there.

85
00:03:12.830 --> 00:03:14.789
So you can get a larger brush.

86
00:03:14.789 --> 00:03:17.069
You just need to increase this brush size

87
00:03:17.069 --> 00:03:18.229
a little bit bigger.

88
00:03:18.229 --> 00:03:19.710
Couple of caveats to this though.

89
00:03:19.710 --> 00:03:21.870
Once you do that,

90
00:03:21.870 --> 00:03:25.270
you might run into instances of your landscape

91
00:03:25.270 --> 00:03:26.990
running very slow once you've clicked.

92
00:03:26.990 --> 00:03:29.990
So just keep that in mind that the larger your brush goes,

93
00:03:29.990 --> 00:03:33.430
the longer it's gonna take to process those changes.

94
00:03:33.430 --> 00:03:34.830
Now, what we're gonna do

95
00:03:34.830 --> 00:03:36.469
is we're gonna come over to an area like this

96
00:03:36.469 --> 00:03:38.849
and we're just gonna click.

97
00:03:38.849 --> 00:03:40.270
And you're gonna see here

98
00:03:40.270 --> 00:03:43.469
that I just start to kind of bring up this landscape

99
00:03:43.469 --> 00:03:45.129
in various different ways.

100
00:03:45.129 --> 00:03:48.750
Now, you can see I'm starting to kind of,

101
00:03:48.750 --> 00:03:50.550
build up some ridges here.

102
00:03:50.550 --> 00:03:51.909
Now, one of the other things that we can do

103
00:03:52.469 --> 00:03:54.550
is I am gonna turn on my auto rotate here.

104
00:03:54.550 --> 00:03:57.550
And auto rotate allows you to kind of have this

105
00:03:57.550 --> 00:03:59.189
texture rotate itself

106
00:03:59.189 --> 00:04:01.990
as it's being dragged along the landscape.

107
00:04:01.990 --> 00:04:04.949
And this is really, really, really useful

108
00:04:04.949 --> 00:04:06.909
as we are trying to kind of get some

109
00:04:06.909 --> 00:04:10.550
different looking data using the exact same stamp.

110
00:04:10.550 --> 00:04:11.889
So again, what this is gonna do

111
00:04:11.889 --> 00:04:13.550
is it's gonna allow us to make things

112
00:04:13.550 --> 00:04:16.470
look just a little bit more unique

113
00:04:16.470 --> 00:04:19.490
and a little less similar to everything else

114
00:04:19.490 --> 00:04:20.769
that's going on around it.

115
00:04:20.769 --> 00:04:23.170
So you can see here, I'm adding some stuff.

116
00:04:23.170 --> 00:04:23.990
Let me come over here.

117
00:04:23.990 --> 00:04:25.490
So there's my camera bookmark one.

118
00:04:25.490 --> 00:04:28.889
You can see by just pressing one or two,

119
00:04:28.889 --> 00:04:30.689
I can really quickly get around the map

120
00:04:30.689 --> 00:04:32.689
and see where I want to add

121
00:04:32.689 --> 00:04:35.069
some of these really awesome

122
00:04:35.069 --> 00:04:37.250
looking little mountains here and there.

123
00:04:37.250 --> 00:04:38.930
Also remember, you can press shift

124
00:04:38.930 --> 00:04:41.829
to push stuff down into the landscape as well.

125
00:04:41.829 --> 00:04:44.410
So we can get some really cool looking divots

126
00:04:44.410 --> 00:04:45.870
as well as some peaks.

127
00:04:45.870 --> 00:04:47.769
So what I want everybody to do right now,

128
00:04:47.769 --> 00:04:49.370
I'll spend the next few minutes,

129
00:04:49.370 --> 00:04:50.550
maybe like two or three minutes,

130
00:04:51.230 --> 00:04:52.350
just experimenting with this

131
00:04:52.350 --> 00:04:55.389
and brushes of various strength and size

132
00:04:55.389 --> 00:04:57.550
and go ahead and try to fill out

133
00:04:57.550 --> 00:05:01.389
some of your landscape here with this brush tool,

134
00:05:01.389 --> 00:05:02.589
allowing you to again,

135
00:05:02.589 --> 00:05:05.810
add some really interesting features.

136
00:05:05.810 --> 00:05:09.410
Now, once we have finished adding some features

137
00:05:09.410 --> 00:05:11.370
with the alpha brush,

138
00:05:11.370 --> 00:05:12.850
the next thing that I want to talk about

139
00:05:12.850 --> 00:05:14.490
is the pattern brush.

140
00:05:14.490 --> 00:05:17.290
Now the pattern brush works in a similar way.

141
00:05:17.290 --> 00:05:19.009
We assign a texture,

142
00:05:19.009 --> 00:05:23.209
which we can then display across our entire landscape

143
00:05:23.209 --> 00:05:26.449
and then use that to affect the highs

144
00:05:26.449 --> 00:05:27.449
and the low of our landscape.

145
00:05:27.449 --> 00:05:28.589
So in this case, what we're gonna do

146
00:05:28.589 --> 00:05:30.850
is we're gonna take this image right here,

147
00:05:30.850 --> 00:05:32.170
which is some craters,

148
00:05:32.170 --> 00:05:35.410
and we are going to again, go back to our sculpt tool,

149
00:05:35.410 --> 00:05:36.990
but instead of our alpha,

150
00:05:36.990 --> 00:05:38.769
we're gonna click on our pattern

151
00:05:38.769 --> 00:05:42.509
and then we're gonna assign this crater texture to it.

152
00:05:42.509 --> 00:05:46.689
There are gonna be some similar parameters in this tool,

153
00:05:46.689 --> 00:05:47.949
like we saw in the alpha tool,

154
00:05:47.949 --> 00:05:49.389
but there's also gonna be some things

155
00:05:49.389 --> 00:05:50.629
that are a little bit different.

156
00:05:50.629 --> 00:05:53.870
Primarily the world space, origin,

157
00:05:53.870 --> 00:05:56.949
center texture on origin and repeat size.

158
00:05:56.949 --> 00:05:58.649
What these allow us to do

159
00:05:58.649 --> 00:06:01.750
is control how this particular texture

160
00:06:01.750 --> 00:06:04.750
is laid across our landscape.

161
00:06:04.750 --> 00:06:06.310
And what I mean by that is,

162
00:06:06.310 --> 00:06:08.009
well, here we have an example.

163
00:06:08.009 --> 00:06:11.649
If you can't see this laid out on your landscape,

164
00:06:11.649 --> 00:06:13.310
we can switch over to lighting only,

165
00:06:13.310 --> 00:06:14.889
and then you'll actually be able to see

166
00:06:14.889 --> 00:06:17.009
this is that texture right there.

167
00:06:17.050 --> 00:06:20.149
So what happens when we go to paint this

168
00:06:20.149 --> 00:06:22.589
is we're gonna get something like this.

169
00:06:22.589 --> 00:06:24.290
So we're gonna get these craters

170
00:06:24.290 --> 00:06:26.170
that indent into the ground,

171
00:06:26.170 --> 00:06:27.329
and we can actually paint this

172
00:06:27.329 --> 00:06:28.970
across our entire landscape.

173
00:06:28.970 --> 00:06:30.730
So let's go ahead and look at this in action.

174
00:06:30.730 --> 00:06:32.129
So back over in the editor,

175
00:06:32.129 --> 00:06:33.290
I'm gonna hit control space

176
00:06:33.290 --> 00:06:35.089
to come over to my impact craters,

177
00:06:35.089 --> 00:06:37.889
and I'm going to put those as our texture here.

178
00:06:37.889 --> 00:06:39.050
And there we go.

179
00:06:39.050 --> 00:06:43.009
So let's, and we might need to do some stuff here.

180
00:06:43.009 --> 00:06:47.089
So we are going to turn off our auto rotation.

181
00:06:47.089 --> 00:06:48.750
Oh, and I'm on the wrong thing here.

182
00:06:48.750 --> 00:06:50.529
I need to click on the pattern brush.

183
00:06:50.529 --> 00:06:52.329
There we go, my pattern brush.

184
00:06:52.329 --> 00:06:54.910
And that is more like it.

185
00:06:54.910 --> 00:06:58.410
So we're gonna bring this to use world space.

186
00:06:58.410 --> 00:07:04.720
We're gonna set the repeat size here to 8192.

187
00:07:05.040 --> 00:07:07.779
And for having a little problem seeing it,

188
00:07:07.779 --> 00:07:10.240
so I'm gonna come over here to detail lighting.

189
00:07:10.240 --> 00:07:11.079
And there we go.

190
00:07:11.079 --> 00:07:12.620
We can see this just a little bit better here.

191
00:07:12.620 --> 00:07:15.009
So if I was to click on this,

192
00:07:15.009 --> 00:07:18.769
and we'll come back over here to just our regular lit mode,

193
00:07:18.769 --> 00:07:21.689
you can see there are the little divots

194
00:07:21.689 --> 00:07:23.050
or the little craters that it made.

195
00:07:23.050 --> 00:07:24.170
And you can see it's actually made it

196
00:07:24.170 --> 00:07:25.870
across the entire landscape.

197
00:07:25.870 --> 00:07:28.610
So if we were to come here and, I don't know,

198
00:07:28.610 --> 00:07:31.970
maybe like increase or make this repeat size

199
00:07:31.970 --> 00:07:34.589
a little bit larger and come over to an area like this

200
00:07:34.589 --> 00:07:36.649
and click, you're gonna see that the holes

201
00:07:36.649 --> 00:07:38.930
are gonna get a lot bigger.

202
00:07:38.930 --> 00:07:42.050
So you see here, I have some really big impacts.

203
00:07:42.329 --> 00:07:43.850
And then if I was to take this repeat size

204
00:07:43.850 --> 00:07:44.870
and shrink this down,

205
00:07:44.870 --> 00:07:49.810
I'm gonna get these much smaller little holes right there.

206
00:07:49.810 --> 00:07:51.990
So very, very cool stuff going on right there.

207
00:07:51.990 --> 00:07:56.399
So again, like with our last texture input,

208
00:07:56.399 --> 00:07:57.240
our alpha brush,

209
00:07:57.240 --> 00:07:58.759
I want everybody to spend the next few minutes

210
00:07:58.759 --> 00:08:01.199
just adjusting the rotation,

211
00:08:01.199 --> 00:08:03.240
the repeat size and the brush size,

212
00:08:03.240 --> 00:08:06.839
and then coming through and painting on your landscape here

213
00:08:06.839 --> 00:08:08.759
to see the effects that this will have

214
00:08:08.759 --> 00:08:10.620
on your landscape.
